[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:55. Not a Gold Mine]
[00:00.580]Passage 55 | 文章五十五
[00:03.035]Not a gold mine. | 不是金矿。
[00:06.395]Dreams of finding lost treasure almost came true recently. | 寻找失落宝藏的梦想最近几乎成真。
[00:13.175]A new machine called the Revealer has been invented, | 一台名为“揭示者”的新机器已被发明，
[00:18.335]and it has been used to detect gold which has been buried in the ground. | 它已被用于探测埋在地下的黄金。
[00:24.540]The machine was used in a cave near the seashore, | 这台机器被用于海边附近的一个洞穴中，
[00:29.105]where, it is said, pirates used to hide gold. | 据说，海盗们曾藏匿黄金。
[00:34.220]The pirates would often bury gold in the cave and then fail to collect it. | 海盗们经常将黄金埋藏在洞穴中，然后未能将其取走。
[00:42.170]Armed with the new machine, a search party went into the cave, | 装备了这台新机器，一支搜寻队进入洞穴，
[00:47.505]hoping to find buried treasure. | 希望找到埋藏的宝藏。
[00:50.760]The leader of the party was examining the soil near the entrance to the cave, | 队伍的领队正在检查洞穴入口附近的泥土，
[00:57.100]when the machine showed that there was gold under the ground. | 这时机器显示地下有黄金。
[01:02.270]Very excited, the party dug a hole two feet deep. | 非常兴奋，队伍挖了一个两英尺深的洞。
[01:07.305]They finally found a small gold coin, | 他们最终找到了一枚小金币，
[01:11.665]which was almost worthless. | 几乎一文不值。
[01:14.360]The party then searched the whole cave thoroughly, | 队伍随后彻底搜查了整个洞穴，
[01:18.365]but did not find anything except an empty tin trunk. | 但除了一个空锡箱外，一无所获。
[01:23.580]In spite of this, many people are confident that the Revealer may reveal something of value fairly soon. | 尽管如此，许多人仍相信“揭示者”可能很快会揭示出一些有价值的东西。